    MOD_DESC = "[h1]China Railway FXN5C Diesel Locomotive[/h1]\nChina Railway blue, Jinwen Railway and a separate red FXN5C 0001 prototype for Transport Fever 2: eleven numbered locomotives.\n\n[h2]v0.44 update[/h2]\nThe red 0001 has its own cab, four upper headlights, vertically paired lower lamps, revised doors/ladders and raised metallic lettering. This update fixes the cab-corner transition planes, continuous raked window profile, black cab divider and vertical front handrails. Production locomotives gain refined roof panels, exhaust/grille divisions, recessed rectangular windscreens, covered horns and thicker sandboxes. Fuxing lettering uses a lower-right shadow; CR/prototype waist stripes are warmer orange-yellow.\nAll purchase icons now show a horizontal whole-locomotive side view with a simple track display. The missing prototype TGA paths are supplied: 52 images cover all numbered models and the two production groups, at two UI sizes and standard/high density.\nFans rotate; large louvers remain open at 55 degrees; smaller louvers use a 0.8-second top-to-bottom wave, up to 40 degrees, with nine larger blades per window at near LOD. All-animation, fans-only and static options remain available. Reload after changing options. These are display settings, not thermal simulation.\n[url=https://github.com/Manfredss/fxn5c-tpf2/releases/tag/v0.44]Full changes, previews, game package and editable SourceKits[/url]\n\n[h2]Contents[/h2]\nChina Railway: 0051, 0066 (Shanghai); 0096, 0102 (Nanjing East); 0057, 0081 (Hangzhou); 0035, 0115 (Xuzhou).\nJinwen Railway: 7005, 7006.\nRed prototype: 0001, a separate purchase entry outside the two production groups. Search for 0001 or Red Prototype.\n\n[h2]In-game configuration[/h2]\nPower: 3530 kW. Tractive effort: 580 kN. Top speed: 120 km/h. Weight: 150 t.\nAll years by default; optionally keep CR 2024/Jinwen 2025 availability. The prototype currently has no year restriction and temporarily reuses production performance. Depot markings, dates and parameters are project configurations, not certified vehicle histories.\n\n[h2]Validation and limitations[/h2]\nNative/static, source-consistency, local geometry and icon checks passed. Systematic in-game/Model Editor testing is pending; prototype purchase visibility needs confirmation after a full game restart. Project previews are offline renders.\nThis is a reference-based reconstruction, not factory CAD. Bogies, coupling compatibility and cab interiors remain approximate. Linkage rods use deforming skinning; prototype access ladders may interfere at larger steering angles. Extreme curves, hidden structures and directional lights need further game testing. Per-number leading inner-lamp colors are custom configurations.\n\n[h2]Editable models and community refinement[/h2]\n[url=https://github.com/Manfredss/fxn5c-tpf2]Source files, issues and contribution guide[/url]\nThe v0.44 prototype SourceKit includes its v0.43 baseline. A separate v0.42 full SourceKit provides the editable production models in the same v0.44 Release. No new FBX is included; historical FBXs represent v0.24 only. The incremental build has historical dependencies and has not been certified as a clean, one-command rebuild. Read the build guide first.\n\n[h2]License[/h2]\nOriginal models, textures and asset data: CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 (attribution, noncommercial, share alike). You may modify and share noncommercial adaptations under that license without asking each time. Credit the project, link the license and describe changes.\nOriginal program logic: MIT (commercial code use permitted, not commercial model use). Third-party railway marks, font designs and reference materials are excluded. See the repository license scope and notices.\n\n[h2]Credits and feedback[/h2]\nProject initiator/reviewer: Manfredss / [ihtw] DisguiseMyse1f. AI-assisted procedural modeling and scripting were used. Thanks to reference contributors; Dreamrail illustrations informed structural reconstruction. Reference images are not distributed. This is not an official manufacturer, railway-operator or Dreamrail release.\nBack up saves, fully restart after updating, clear purchase filters and avoid enabling duplicate local/Workshop copies. Please report version, number, reproduction steps and screenshots. Improvements to bogies, linkages, paint and testing are welcome!\n",
